VOLATILITY REGIMES (based on ATR z-score):
- LOW (z-score < {{ volatility_low_threshold }}): Market quiet. Stops may be tight. Only trade with high conviction.
- NORMAL (z-score {{ volatility_low_threshold }} to {{ volatility_high_threshold }}): Standard conditions. Use 1.0-{{ max_stop_atr }} ATR stops. Standard position sizing.
- HIGH (z-score {{ volatility_high_threshold }} to {{ volatility_extreme_threshold }}): Elevated volatility. Use the wide end of the range, 1.25-{{ max_stop_atr }} ATR stops (never above the {{ max_stop_atr }}x cap). Position size halved automatically by the system.
- EXTREME (z-score > {{ volatility_extreme_threshold }}): Dangerous conditions. Only trade with very high conviction. The routing layer raises the confluence gate for this regime; report your raw score and let the gate decide.
